\documentclass[dvipdfm]{book}
\newcommand{\VolumeName}{Volume 7.1: Axiom Hyperdoc Pages}
\input{bookheader.tex}
\pagenumbering{arabic}
\mainmatter
\setcounter{chapter}{0} % Chapter 1
\chapter{Introduction}
This book contains the pages which will be displayed by HyperDoc.
The code for HyperDoc is in Volume 7\cite{Book07}

\section{Setting up the Hyperdoc fonts and colors}
For these images we used the following settings in the X11 resouces.
\begin{chunk}{Xresource.txt}
Axiom.hyperdoc.RmFont: -adobe-courier-medium-r-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.RmColor: black
Axiom.hyperdoc.ActiveFont: -adobe-courier-bold-r-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.ActiveColor: blue
Axiom.hyperdoc.AxiomFont: -adobe-courier-bold-o-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.AxiomColor: blue
Axiom.hyperdoc.BoldFont: -adobe-courier-bold-r-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.BoldColor: blue
Axiom.hyperdoc.TtFont: -adobe-courier-medium-r-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.TtColor: blue
Axiom.hyperdoc.EmphasizeFont: -adobe-courier-medium-o-normal--18-*-*-*-m-*-iso8859-1
Axiom.hyperdoc.EmphasizeColor: red
Axiom.hyperdoc.InputBackground: black
Axiom.hyperdoc.InputForeground: yellow
Axiom.hyperdoc.BorderColor: black
Axiom.hyperdoc.Background: PaleGoldenrod
\end{chunk}

To enable these you can create a file containing the above lines which,
by convention, is called {\tt .XResource} in your home directory of the 
machine where you will VIEW the files (not from where they are running).
The file name is just a convention so here we will use {\tt Xresource.txt}

To enable these type
\begin{verbatim}
   xrdb -merge Xresource.txt
\end{verbatim}

If you prefer a different font you can list the fonts on your system
using the command
\begin{verbatim}
   xlsfonts
\end{verbatim}

