                               -x --'
                        K (x)=e   >   d T (t) , where t=x-3;
                         1        --   r r
                                  r=0

          For x>4,

                               -x
                              e   --'                    9-x
                       K (x)= --- >   e T (t) , where t= ---.
                        1         --   r r               1+x
                              \/x r=0

                                   1
          For x near zero, K (x)~= -. This approximation is used when x is
                            1      x
          sufficiently small for the result to be correct to machine
