\chapter{Page hierarchy layout}
This is the forest of pages in hyperdoc. Any page at the leftmost
margin is a root page. Notice that the roots are disconnnected.
The only reachable pages are those from the "RootPage" page below.
All others exist but cannot be reached.

Indentation implies that a page can be reached by the less indented page.

Pages which have vertical bars or parens around them are lisp calls.
